{"agent_id":"pp3g-Fdp6-logic-review-of-liveness-tooling-under-epic-423-e5d4","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T00:18:35.088985337Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"30fe1518-83b9-482d-ad39-5554a2a31c71","comment_uuid":"3ff6f3e9-9bb4-4bb5-ad4a-8e396ab87ba6","author":"pp3g-Fdp6-logic-review-of-liveness-tooling-under-epic-423-e5d4","content":"## LOGIC REVIEW — Liveness tooling under EPIC #423 (agent-liveness.py v2 + watchdog v2)\n\nAnchored to #435 (v2 passed code-verification). This review attacks DESIGN/LOGIC, not code correctness. Code read in full: scripts/agent-liveness.py (594 lines). Watchdog assessed from its spec in #423 (00:05 plan by pp3g-pfpM): detached 120s loop running agent-liveness.py --json --all, appending one compacted JSON line/cycle to /tmp/opencode/liveness-log.jsonl, diffing verdicts vs /tmp/opencode/liveness-state/watchdog-state.json, posting [WATCHDOG] comments on change (new LIKELY-FROZEN/STALE-SUSPECT, or ALIVE->SESSION-GONE vanish), dedupe by per-agent last_flagged_verdict with re-flag on severity worsening or post-recovery new episode.\n\nOVERALL JUDGMENT: SOUND-WITH-CAVEATS. Core engine is structurally sound (MECE matrix, real fix for Bug-A/Bug-B). Caveats are signal-validity + watchdog-robustness gaps, not correctness bugs. Tool WOULD surface all five tonight-hangs but misclassifies cause for the rate-limit class and predicts no pre-death. Not a redesign.\n\n### FINDINGS (aspect | assessment | failure-mode | recommendation | severity)\n\n[A1] VERDICT MATRIX — structure is MECE\n- Assessment: classify() (agent-liveness.py:395-410) is a strict if/elif chain -> 6 classes mutually exclusive by construction; every (status x aliveness x role x pane_frozen x age) combo maps to exactly one verdict -> collectively exhaustive over discrete input domains.\n- Failure-mode: none structural.\n- Recommendation: none. Severity: — (positive)\n\n[A1b] VERDICT MATRIX — DONE overrides aliveness (contract violation)\n- Assessment: `if status == \"DONE\": return \"DONE-CONFIRMED\"` (line 399) trusts the sentinel absolutely, contradicting the module's own invariant \"v2 never trusts the sentinel alone; it cross-checks against process aliveness\" (lines 16, 48). A process that wrote DONE but is still ALIVE (hung in post-DONE cleanup, or wrote DONE erroneously) is hidden as DONE-CONFIRMED.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE NEGATIVE — hung-after-DONE zombie invisible; exactly the class v2 was built to catch.\n- Recommendation: when status==DONE AND aliveness==ALIVE, still inspect pane_frozen; if frozen emit a distinct DONE-BUT-ALIVE warning. At minimum document the override + blind spot.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER (high)\n\n[A1c] VERDICT MATRIX — LIKELY-FROZEN precedence over STALE-SUSPECT\n- Assessment: pane_frozen short-circuits to LIKELY-FROZEN regardless of age (lines 406-407). An ALIVE agent FRESH (age<2xbudget) but static-pane between two 120s samples (long tool call, slow think, no output flush) is flagged LIKELY-FROZEN.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE POSITIVE — healthy agent mislabeled frozen.\n- Recommendation: require age>=budget (or pane_frozen across >=2 consecutive cycles + min age floor) before LIKELY-FROZEN; else keep RUNNING-ALIVE, record pane-static as soft hint.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A2] SIGNAL VALIDITY — mtime != progress\n- Assessment: walk-mtime only reflects worktree filesystem writes. \"Thinking\" (LLM inference, tool calls not writing the worktree) and long external tool waits produce NO mtime change and may produce NO pane change.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE POSITIVE — the exact mode the brief calls out: legitimately-thinking/slow agent with static pane + old mtimes -> STALE-SUSPECT (or LIKELY-FROZEN).\n- Recommendation: (1) shorten default budget or make per-role; (2) add progress signal beyond mtime — agent heartbeat, LLM token-stream liveness, or crosslink issue-comment recency; (3) pair mtime+pane-hash with hysteresis.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A2b] SIGNAL VALIDITY — rate-limit parking indistinguishable from hang\n- Assessment: muse agents parked on retry-after (backoff to 00:00:00Z daily reset) are ALIVE (event loop live; hourly cleanup heartbeats prove it) but write nothing and show static pane. Tool sees exactly STALE-SUSPECT/LIKELY-FROZEN, no way to know INTENTIONAL wait resuming at midnight.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE POSITIVE (misclassified cause) — 4 of tonight's 5 hangs are this class; tool would alarm them as \"hangs\" when they are \"expected parking.\"\n- Recommendation: detect parking explicitly — scrape opencode.log for AI_APICallError/retry-after, or agent emits parked-until=<ts> sentinel; classify PARKED (informational, no alert) not STALE-SUSPECT. Highest-value signal-validity fix.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER (high)\n\n[A2c] SIGNAL VALIDITY — process-aliveness != progress\n- Assessment: _non_shell_descendants (lines 310-327) proves a non-shell process exists, but a process can be ALIVE yet deadlocked/wedged (kJSL invisible-churn loop, or stream awaiting unresponsive peer). Scan sees node/opencode -> ALIVE.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE NEGATIVE for pre-death degeneration — cannot flag \"looping uselessly\"/\"wedged\" until process exits.\n- Recommendation: accept aliveness as necessary-not-sufficient; pair with [A2] progress signals; document STALE-SUSPECT/LIKELY-FROZEN as only coarse pre-death hints.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A2d] SIGNAL VALIDITY — role recovery fragility\n- Assessment: ROLE_RE (line 113) matches only `--agent 'role'` (single-quoted). Double-quoted `--agent \"role\"` NOT matched -> role=unknown -> conservative DEAD-UNMARKED (mislabels finished reviewer/auditor as zombie). Scrollback can also scroll past launch line on long sessions.\n- Failure-mode: FALSE POSITIVE on FINISHED-UNMARKABLE when role undetectable.\n- Recommendation: accept both quote styles; prefer robust \"finished\" signal — presence of a result/handoff comment on the agent's issue — over scrollback role.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A3] WATCHDOG — crash / self-liveness (single point of failure)\n- Assessment: detached tmux loop has no supervisor. If it dies (OOM, tmux-server exit, session killed) monitoring silently stops; nothing restarts it. Mid-write kill truncates jsonl line and can corrupt watchdog-state.json (no atomic write specified for watchdog's own state file, unlike agent-liveness.py:385 os.replace).\n- Failure-mode: MISSED EVENTS + corrupt state after crash; silent monitoring gap — watchdog is the alerting path, its death blinds the whole story.\n- Recommendation: (1) atomic os.replace for watchdog-state.json; (2) meta-watchdog / systemd timer or PID-file guard refusing second instance + restart on death; (3) graceful corrupt-state handling (reseed, don't crash).\n- Severity: MUST-CONSIDER\n\n[A3b] WATCHDOG — dedupe / spam on oscillation\n- Assessment: spec re-flags on \"severity worsening OR after recovery new episode.\" Agent oscillating STALE<->ALIVE every cycle (borderline writer, pane flicker) re-flags every other cycle -> spam. No hysteresis/debounce.\n- Failure-mode: SPAM — operator drowned in repeated [WATCHDOG] comments.\n- Recommendation: require N consecutive stale/frozen cycles (2-3) before first flag; after recovery require quiet period before new episode; debounce pane-frozen toggles.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A3c] WATCHDOG — vanish detection needs aliveness, not just verdict\n- Assessment: spec stores last_flagged_verdict and flags ALIVE->SESSION-GONE. But agent-liveness.py renders a vanished session as DEAD-UNMARKED/FINISHED-UNMARKABLE (NOT in STALE-SUSPECT/LIKELY-FROZEN flag set). Vanish must be detected from aliveness-field transition, requiring watchdog state to track aliveness (or infer via verdict transition RUNNING/STALE/FROZEN -> DEAD/FINISHED). Storing only last_flagged_verdict is insufficient unless verdict-transition inference implemented.\n- Failure-mode: MISSED vanish alert if implemented naively.\n- Recommendation: explicitly store previous aliveness per agent; flag prev=ALIVE & curr=SESSION-GONE; document as distinct rule from severity-worsening.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER (spec ambiguity -> implementation risk)\n\n[A3d] WATCHDOG — alert routing + unbounded log\n- Assessment: spec posts [WATCHDOG] to issue #429 (a research issue), mixing all-agent liveness into one unrelated issue; no per-agent routing. jsonl grows unbounded (~720 lines/day, no rotation).\n- Failure-mode: (1) alert fatigue / wrong audience on #429; (2) disk fill over weeks.\n- Recommendation: route to dedicated liveness issue (or agent's own issue); add jsonl rotation/retention.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A4] CADENCE — 120s poll fine; 90min stale budget too coarse\n- Assessment: 120s polling catches process EXIT within one cycle (good). But STALE-SUSPECT only fires at age>=2xbudget=90min (default budget 45). Tonight's hangs were quiet 85-96 min before operator detection — 90min threshold roughly matches, does NOT beat operator. Lever for \"earlier\" is budget, not poll interval.\n- Failure-mode: cannot catch hangs materially EARLIER than operator (stale threshold ~= observed freeze duration).\n- Recommendation: shorten default budget (15-20min -> 30-40min stale) and/or per-role; keep 120s poll. Pair with [A2b] so shorter budget doesn't just add false positives.\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER\n\n[A5] CONCEPTUAL — FINISHED-UNMARKABLE vs DEAD-UNMARKED\n- Assessment: split IS useful — cleanup treats both removable, but orchestration differs: FINISHED-UNMARKABLE (read-only role, done) -> no relaunch; DEAD-UNMARKED (builder/unknown, zombie) -> likely incomplete, investigate/relaunch. Taxonomy earns its keep for routing.\n- Failure-mode: differentiator is scrollback role, fragile ([A2d]) -> finished reviewer with undetectable role mislabeled DEAD-UNMARKED (still flagged, wrong routing). DEAD-UNMARKED also conflates \"crashed mid-task (incomplete)\" with \"crashed after completing (forgot DONE)\".\n- Recommendation: KEEP the split (justified) BUT derive \"finished\" from robust signal — result/handoff comment on agent's issue — not scrollback role. Do NOT collapse (loses relaunch-vs-leave signal).\n- Severity: SHOULD-CONSIDER (taxonomy sound; implementation signal fragile)","created_at":"2026-08-24T00:18:35.081889106Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:N2MKNhC24y9CrvAmIsloNCwW+yR3ND/cHGCpBawbvQc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgjRheorzkSr9SfTBgosQr/VKNecNMMWzQOuLX+IxysRMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAhdZonGXKEIfOFoulRds5BwpzrD/Xfc3bjmEbCHbj8JIDbgR4ElcuT8cXi/ttyXx9Rcd+XZ+63Rop5yVEORBqCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:N2MKNhC24y9CrvAmIsloNCwW+yR3ND/cHGCpBawbvQc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgjRheorzkSr9SfTBgosQr/VKNecNMMWzQOuLX+IxysRMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJfKcuisuS1gxy1gBA/jpBwrZpG/L0e+QelB/PvCF3mR0B/oghoeaCqovubGvc2DcIQArYzueIcwEzQhG4LHFgY="}
